Feature: Map tools
  On: desktop
  When you drag the tactical map, it pans. PLAN and GOTO change what a click on the map does.
  With PLAN, a click adds a waypoint to the plan. With GOTO, a click sends the plane to that
  point. Press the same tool again to go back to panning.

  Expectation: PLAN picks the planning tool
    Given the map tool is not PLAN
    When the operator toggles the planning tool
    Then the map tool is PLAN

  Expectation: PLAN again goes back to panning
    Given the map tool is PLAN
    When the operator toggles the planning tool
    Then the map tool is pan

  Expectation: GOTO picks the fly-to tool
    Given the map tool is not GOTO
    When the operator toggles the fly-to tool
    Then the map tool is GOTO

  Expectation: A GOTO click flies the plane there
    The plane flies to the point at its current altitude, and then it circles the point in
    [[GUIDED]]. The map goes back to panning.
    Given the map tool is GOTO
    And the vehicle is armed
    When the operator clicks the map
    Then the autopilot mode is GUIDED
    And the map tool is pan
